ource_file\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/ayah-activation/v12-tr/s029/full_context_packet.json\"}},\"bundle_type\":\"ayah\",\"butuncul_okuma_line\":null,\"channel_generated_outputs\":{\"files\":[{\"bytes\":25098445,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/channel_candidates.jsonl\",\"role\":\"channel_candidates.jsonl\"},{\"bytes\":655282,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/channel_candidates.tsv\",\"role\":\"channel_candidates.tsv\"},{\"bytes\":14909,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/summary.json\",\"role\":\"summary.json\"},{\"bytes\":11912557,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/families/candidate_graphs.jsonl\",\"role\":\"families/candidate_graphs.jsonl\"},{\"bytes\":280175,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/families/candidate_similarity_edges.tsv\",\"role\":\"families/candidate_similarity_edges.tsv\"},{\"bytes\":2143256,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/families/channel_families.jsonl\",\"role\":\"families/channel_families.jsonl\"},{\"bytes\":26945,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/families/candidate_family_membership.tsv\",\"role\":\"families/candidate_family_membership.tsv\"},{\"bytes\":743329,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/families/family_branch_inventory.tsv\",\"role\":\"families/family_branch_inventory.tsv\"},{\"bytes\":9274,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/families/consolidation_summary.json\",\"role\":\"families/consolidation_summary.json\"},{\"bytes\":27898,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/paths/path_summary.json\",\"role\":\"paths/path_summary.json\"},{\"bytes\":90274886,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/paths/path_families/semantic_path_families.jsonl\",\"role\":\"paths/path_families/semantic_path_families.jsonl\"},{\"bytes\":16758877,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/paths/path_families/path_similarity_edges.tsv\",\"role\":\"paths/path_families/path_similarity_edges.tsv\"},{\"bytes\":11448,\"compressed\":false,\"path\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029/paths/path_families/path_family_summary.json\",\"role\":\"paths/path_families/path_family_summary.json\"}],\"source_dir\":\"quran-data/data/analysis/channels/network-v3/s029\",\"usage\":\"External source manifest only. These generated outputs may inform channel-family/path context when the agent has file access, but first-pass review limits still apply: no established channel name, accept/reject claim, or maturity claim unless a future adjudicated ledger is present.\"},\"channel_subchannels_anchored_here\":[{\"active_motifs\":\"crossing a distance or water `quranic:root_001240:B003/m01`; a stranded traveler whose means fail `quranic:root_001240:B006/m01`; highway seizure and obstruction `quranic:root_001240:B023/m01`; an extended traversable road `quranic:root_000672:B001/m01`; road users and travelers `quranic:root_000672:B002/m01`; preventing and turning away `quranic:root_000848:B001/m01`; a route leading to water `quranic:root_000848:B004/m01`; a worked road `quranic:root_001046:B011/m01`; walkers on foot `quranic:root_000546:B003/m01`\",\"ayah_anchors\":\"ق ط ع 29:29; س ب ل 29:29,38; ص د د 29:38; ع م ل 29:38; ر ج ل 29:29.\",\"ayah_refs\":[\"29:29\",\"29:38\"],\"key\":\"A\",\"name\":\"Cutting the Worked Road\",\"parent_channel\":\"P3 (29:28-44) Routes and Forums Turned Hostile\",\"parent_semantic_invariant\":\"Shared channels for movement and speech are converted from public access into mechanisms of obstruction and abuse.\",\"parent_surprising_reach\":\"The passage links highway robbery, worked tracks, water access, public council, loud circulation, and the restraint or excess of the tongue.\",\"reading_type\":\"mixed\",\"scene_or_process\":\"Travelers move on a known track toward resources until an obstacle, seizure, or exhausted means interrupts passage.\",\"synthesis\":\"Cutting the road is a full disruption of public mobility: a known worked track and its resource route are blocked until the traveler becomes \\\"cut off\\\" through lost mount, food, or money. The lexical assembly makes obstruction an attack on the infrastructure that lets strangers continue.\"},{\"active_motifs\":\"dwelling and nightly shelter `quranic:root_000166:B001/m01`; crosspieces carrying a house-post `quranic:root_001222:B008/m01`; fitted joint, socket, or door fitting `quranic:root_000347:B011/m01`; standing tool or structural member `quranic:root_001273:B012/m01`; residence as a stable place `quranic:root_000726:B002/m01`; joining two skins or wall-halves `quranic:root_000121:B006/m01`\",\"ayah_anchors\":\"ب ي ت 29:41; ق ر ي 29:31,34; ح ق ق 29:44; ق و م 29:28-30,35-36; س ك ن 29:38; ب ص ر 29:38.\",\"ayah_refs\":[\"29:41\",\"29:31\",\"29:44\",\"29:28\",\"29:38\"],\"key\":\"A\",\"name\":\"Fitted Dwelling Structure\",\"parent_channel\":\"P3 (29:28-44) House, Household, and Failed Support\",\"parent_semantic_invariant\":\"A dwelling is viable only when fitted structure, inhabited relations, and load-bearing supports work together.\",\"parent_surprising_reach\":\"The spider comparison opens into joinery, tent supports, stitched panels, household membership, bodily ribs, hidden pain, and timber-eating decay.\",\"reading_type\":\"latent/lexical\",\"scene_or_process\":\"A shelter is assembled from a standing support, a fitted socket or joint, transverse members, and joined wall material.\",\"synthesis\":\"The house is a fitted mechanism, not merely an enclosure. Posts, crosspieces, sockets, and joined skins distribute load; the spider-house pressures the comparison by offering the name of shelter without dependable structural work.\"},{\"active_motifs\":\"kin and co-inhabitants `quranic:root_000064:B001/m01`; qualification for a role or place `quranic:root_000064:B003/m01`; inhabited familiarity `quranic:root_000064:B004/m01`; household and dependents `quranic:root_000166:B002/m01`; residents of a house `quranic:root_000726:B003/m01`; what gives inward familiarity and calm `quranic:root_000726:B004/m01`; gathered town and townspeople `quranic:root_001222:B001/m01`; hospitality through gathered food `quranic:root_001222:B003/m01`\",\"ayah_anchors\":\"ء ه ل 29:31-34; ب ي ت 29:41; س ك ن 29:38; ق ر ي 29:31,34.\",\"ayah_refs\":[\"29:31\",\"29:41\",\"29:38\"],\"key\":\"B\",\"name\":\"Household, Inhabitants, and Welcome\",\"parent_channel\":\"P3 (29:28-44) House, Household, and Failed Support\",\"parent_semantic_invariant\":\"A dwelling is viable only when fitted structure, inhabited relations, and load-bearing supports work together.\",\"parent_surprising_reach\":\"The spider comparison opens into joinery, tent supports, stitched panels, household membership, bodily ribs, hidden pain, and timber-eating decay.\",\"reading_type\":\"mixed\",\"scene_or_process\":\"Kin, residents, and guests are gathered by a dwelling whose social function is recognition, qualification, and safe reception.\",\"synthesis\":\"\\\"Household\\\" names more than blood descent: it is a relation of residence, qualification, familiarity, and welcome. The repeated negotiation over Lot's family therefore asks who truly belongs inside a protective social dwelling.\"},{\"active_motifs\":\"manifest sign `quranic:root_000074:B003/m01`; retained route-guiding landmark `quranic:root_001040:B002/m02`; emergence into visible clarity `quranic:root_000170:B004/m01`; gestural clarification `quranic:root_000170:B005/m02`; inward sight and evidentiary understanding `quranic:root_000121:B002/m01`; retained trace after departure `quranic:root_000180:B002/m01`\",\"ayah_anchors\":\"ء ي ي 29:35,44; ع ل م 29:28,32,41-43; ب ي ن 29:35,38-39; ب ص ر 29:38; ت ر ك 29:35.\",\"ayah_refs\":[\"29:35\",\"29:28\",\"29:38\"],\"key\":\"A\",\"name\":\"Mark, Landmark, and Inward Sight\",\"parent_channel\":\"P3 (29:28-44) Examples Made Legible\",\"parent_semantic_invariant\":\"A truth becomes cognitively usable when it is marked, modeled, and impressed into a form that can restrain mistaken judgment.\",\"parent_surprising_reach\":\"Parable-making behaves like heraldry, model-making, molding, and tethering: cognition is given a durable form and then held to it.\",\"reading_type\":\"mixed\",\"scene_or_process\":\"A distinguishing trace remains in the landscape, directs attention, and becomes inward recognition rather than bare looking.\",\"synthesis\":\"The \\\"clear sign\\\" left from the town is a trace that functions like a landmark: it first catches sight, then opens meaning, then becomes inward evidence. Remains are useful because they preserve direction after the event itself has departed.\"}],\"coverage\":{\"branch_inventories\":{\"present\":true,\"scope\":\"surah-fallback-scoped-to-ayah\",\"scoping\":{\"applied\":true,\"ayah_roots_from_qac\":[\"بصر\",\"بين\",\"زين\",\"سبل\",\"سكن\",\"شطن\",\"صدد\",\"عمل\",\"عود\",\"كون\"],\"channel_citations_found\":29,\"citations_unresolvable_in_surah_inventory\":[],\"dropped_roots\":[\"س م و\",\"ء ل ه\",\"ر ح م\",\"ح س ب\",\"ن و س\",\"ق و ل\",\"ء م ن\",\"ف ت ن\",\"ق ب ل\",\"ص د ق\",\"ك ذ ب\",\"س و ء\",\"س ب ق\",\"ح ك م\",\"ر ج و\",\"ل ق ي\",\"ء ج ل\",\"ء ت ي\",\"س م ع\",\"ج ه د\",\"ن ف س\",\"غ ن ي\",\"ص ل ح\",\"ك ف ر\",\"ج ز ي\",\"ح س ن\",\"و ص ي\",\"ء ن س\",\"و ل د\",\"ش ر ك\",\"ل ي س\",\"ط و ع\",\"ر ج ع\",\"ن ب ء\",\"د خ ل\",\"ء ذ ي\",\"ج ع ل\",\"ع ذ ب\",\"ج ي ء\",\"ن ص ر\",\"ر ب ب\",\"ص د ر\",\"ن ف ق\",\"ت ب ع\",\"ح م ل\",\"خ ط ء\",\"ش ي ء\",\"ث ق ل\",\"س ء ل\",\"ي و م\",\"ف ر ي\",\"ر س ل\",\"ل ب ث\",\"ء ل ف\",\"س ن و\",\"خ م س\",\"ع و م\",\"ء خ ذ\",\"ط و ف\",\"ظ ل م\",\"ن ج و\",\"ص ح ب\",\"س ف ن\",\"ع ب د\",\"و ق ي\",\"خ ي ر